sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant C as BrokenCollector
  participant F as BrokenFinder
  participant S as AssessmentStore
  participant A as Assessor
  participant Q as Quarantine
  participant K as BackupMirror
  participant B as BrokenReview
  participant E as RepairEncoder
  participant D as DownloaderDatabase
  U->>C: broken --collect
  C->>C: QuarantineSet: read every _broken below PATH
  C->>F: find()
  F-->>C: (path, reason) from shrink.db / report, not held anywhere
  loop each video
    C->>S: stored(path)?
    alt unchanged (size, mtime, method)
      S-->>C: stored Assessment
    else new or changed or --recheck
      C->>A: assess(path)
      A-->>C: Assessment (decodes, still, errors, class)
      C->>S: put(path, assessment)
    end
  end
  C->>C: false alarms (healthy): clear BROKEN entry, not moved
  C->>U: plan, confirm?
  U-->>C: y
  loop each damaged video
    C->>Q: collect(path, assessment, reason)
    Q->>Q: rename every hard link name into _broken/<class>/...
  end
  C->>K: unavailable(root)?
  alt backup disk available
    C->>K: check(names): same path, then search by name
    K-->>C: intact / damaged / missing (full decode of each copy)
    C->>Q: note_backup(item, result)
  else not mounted
    C->>U: backup check pending - mount the disk
  end
  U->>B: broken --review (terminal or GUI dialog)
  loop promising (most usable first), then hopeless
    B->>U: measurement, backup state, choice?
    alt not checked yet
      U-->>B: c
      B->>K: check(names)
    else intact copy
      U-->>B: b
      B->>Q: recover(item): copy from the backup under all names
    else no intact copy: repair
      B->>E: encode(held, repaired-<name>)
      E-->>B: validated (full decode without errors)
      U-->>B: accept
      B->>Q: install(item, repaired)
    else keep
      B->>Q: release (not damaged) or restore (kept after review)
    else no intact copy: delete
      B->>Q: delete(item)
      B->>D: reset(original)
    end
  end
